From 4a26e93ec41aa92a068ad81964c720e0eca709e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:11:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] S5: accept devicebasedauth.org credentials and access
 tokens as API keys
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The auth middleware tries devicebasedauth.org first for `Authorization: DBA`
(+ DPoP) and for Bearer tokens whose JWS header typ is dba-access+jwt; any
other Bearer is still a Clerk session. createSiteAuth (audience cronly.org,
namespace cronly, scopes USER_SCOPES) is kept per issuer at module scope so
JWKS, status-list and DPoP replay caches persist per isolate; linkedUser
reaches the request's bindings through AsyncLocalStorage.

The result is { account, key_id: <credential id>, scopes, session: false,
dba: { account, device_id, credential_id } }. The AccountDO must confirm
the link (dba-authenticate) and records the credential's expiry and monthly
cap. Because the credential id is the key id, API-key metering, holds and
key budgets apply unchanged: GET reads cost 21 µ$ + 2 µ$/job, and the
grant's spend_usd_per_month becomes a UTC-month key budget in µ$ that
queued retries re-check (unlink refuses them). cronly:session deliberately
does not grant SESSION. /mcp forwards the verified identity to its
in-process tool requests because a DPoP proof is single use.

OpenAPI gains the DeviceCredential security scheme (regenerated).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
